# Penalty charge numbers

A penalty charge number (PCN) identifies one registration or one received form. It is the case's
**PCN stem** plus a one-digit suffix.

## Stem and suffix

The case stores one stem, set when the case is created and never changed. Case details shows it
above State. Search and the case list use the same value (filter **Penalty charge number stem**,
column **PCN stem**).

Each registration stores a full PCN: the stem plus a suffix. Local seed scripts build the first
registration with `bin/generate-pcn-number.sh`, which always uses suffix `0`. A later registration
uses the stem plus one more than the highest existing registration suffix. A suffix above `9` is
rejected. Case details Registration, and any edit of that registration, use the current row: the
highest suffix, then the latest `created_at`. The Previous registrations tab lists every earlier
registration, lowest suffix first, and leaves the current row out. When there is no earlier row,
the tab says **There are no previous registrations.**

Each TE9, TE7, PE3, and PE2 row stores the full PCN of the registration that was current when the
form was recorded. The same form PCN may be stored more than once.

Stem `WE70599899` with three registrations is `WE705998990`, `WE705998991` (both previous), and
`WE705998992` (current). The design docs page lists the seeded cases that demonstrate this, with
their case numbers, after `bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh`:
[Penalty charge numbers — seeded examples](http://localhost:4567/penalty-charge-numbers.html#seeded-examples).

## Format

```text
AA9999999X9
```

| Part | Length | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `AA` | 2 or 3 letters | Local authority id |
| `9999999` | 7 digits | Unique PCN number for that authority |
| `X` | 1 character | Mod 11 check digit (`0`–`9`, or `A` when the remainder is 10) |
| `9` | 1 digit | Numeric suffix |

The suffix is **not** included in the check-digit calculation. A 2-letter authority produces a
10-character stem and an 11-character PCN (`WE70599899` and `WE705998990`). A 3-letter authority
produces 11 and 12 (`WCC12345670` and `WCC123456700`).

The create API accepts `^[A-Z]{2,3}[0-9]{7}[0-9A]0$` (suffix `0` only). The case then stores the
stem `^[A-Z]{2,3}[0-9]{7}[0-9A]$`. On a registration the file identifier
(`R` + authority id + 5 digits) and batch identifier (`R` + authority id + 6 digits) must use the
same authority id as that registration's PCN.

If the authority id or the 7-digit number is missing, the check digit is not calculated.

## Local authority id

The letters are the TEC authority id, not the CCD FixedList code. `westminster` is `WE`.
`manchesterCityCouncil` is `MC`. The map is `bin/lib/local_authority_pcn_ids.txt`, from the TEC
two-alpha list (Annex 6B). Where an authority has more than one code, the London authorities list
is used when it has one; otherwise the first Annex 6B code is used. Councils with no TEC id are
omitted from the map.

`bin/lib/authority_pcn_id.sh` looks up that file. These scripts then call
`generate-pcn-number.sh` with the id:

| Script | Authority used |
| --- | --- |
| `bin/create-tec-case.sh` | `LOCAL_AUTHORITY`, default `westminster` (`WE`) |
| `bin/create-tec-cases.sh` | Each case's authority (or `LOCAL_AUTHORITY` when set) |
| `bin/create-gm-tec-cases.sh` | Each Greater Manchester authority, via `create-tec-case.sh` |
| `bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh` | Catalogue authority (`LOCAL_AUTHORITY`, default Westminster `WE`) for catalogue PCNs, exception PCNs, and batch identifiers |

Set `PENALTY_CHARGE_NUMBER` on `create-tec-case.sh` to supply a number. File and batch identifiers
then follow that number's authority id unless `FILE_IDENTIFIER` or `BATCH_IDENTIFIER` is set.

## Check digit

The check digit is calculated on the authority id and the 7-digit number only.

### Letter values

Each letter of the authority id becomes a digit. The alphabet restarts at 1 every ten letters.
`J` and `T` are `0`. `Z` is `6`.

| Letters | Values |
| --- | --- |
| A B C D E F G H I J | 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0 |
| K L M N O P Q R S T | 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0 |
| U V W X Y Z | 1 2 3 4 5 6 |

Digits in the 7-digit number stay as themselves.

### Weights

For a 2-letter authority the nine values (2 letters + 7 digits) are weighted 9, 8, … 1:

```text
(a×9) + (b×8) + (c×7) + (d×6) + (e×5) + (f×4) + (g×3) + (h×2) + (i×1)
```

For a 3-letter authority the ten values are weighted 10, 9, … 1:

```text
(a×10) + (b×9) + (c×8) + (d×7) + (e×6) + (f×5) + (g×4) + (h×3) + (i×2) + (j×1)
```

`a` onwards are the characters of the authority id and the 7-digit number, in order, after letters
have been converted.

Divide the total by 11. The remainder is the check digit. If the remainder is 10, the check digit
is `A`.

### Example: `LR2468037`

1. Convert `LR` to digits: `L` is 2, `R` is 8, so `28`.
2. Weight the nine values and add them:

   `(2×9 = 18) + (8×8 = 64) + (2×7 = 14) + (4×6 = 24) + (6×5 = 30) + (8×4 = 32) + (0×3 = 0) + (3×2 = 6) + (7×1 = 7) = 195`

3. Divide 195 by 11. 11 goes into 195 seventeen times (`11×17 = 187`).
4. The remainder is `195 − 187 = 8`, so the check digit is `8`.

With suffix `0` the PCN is `LR246803780`.

### Remainder 10

`LR0000005` totals 87. `87 − (11×7) = 10`, so the check digit is `A` and the PCN is `LR0000005A0`.

### Three-letter authority

`WCC1234567` uses weights 10 down to 1. `W` is 3 and `C` is 3, so the values are
`3, 3, 3, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7`. The total is 165, which divides by 11 exactly. The check digit is
`0` and the PCN is `WCC123456700`.

## Generate a number

```bash
./bin/generate-pcn-number.sh LR 2468037   # LR246803780
./bin/generate-pcn-number.sh WE           # random 7-digit number, check digit, suffix 0
LOCAL_AUTHORITY=manchesterCityCouncil ./bin/create-tec-case.sh -
```
